  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.MongoDBProperties\": {\n        \"summary\": \"A Spring Boot configuration properties class that holds configuration settings pertaining to the MongoDB connection. It is annotated with @ConfigurationProperties(prefix = 'mongodb'), allowing properties prefixed with 'mongodb' (e.g., mongodb.host, mongodb.database) to be automatically bound from application configuration files (such as application.properties or application.yml). It defines two configurable fields: 'host' (defaulting to 'localhost') representing the MongoDB server hostname, and 'database' (defaulting to 'ordering') representing the target database name. Key methods include getHost()/setHost(String) for accessing and setting the MongoDB host, and getDatabase()/setDatabase(String) for accessing and setting the database name. This class enables externalized and environment-specific MongoDB configuration in a Spring Boot application.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/MongoDBProperties.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
